.el .ds Aq '
.TH dedensd 8  "dedensd " 
.SH NAME
dedensd \- A DNS server: a caching forwarder for now.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdedensd\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A DNS server: a caching forwarder for now.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
The configuration file, YAML (D24)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Debug events with \-v, trace events with \-vv
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR [default: json]
How events are written on stderr: one JSON object a line, or text for people
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
text
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
dedensd\-validate(8)
Reads the configuration and builds the pipeline, without binding any socket
.TP
dedensd\-help(8)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
